abstract: >-
  Bangla-SGP is a parallel dataset of human-annotated and rule-augmented
  Bangla sentence–gloss pairs for Bangla Sign Language (BdSL) translation
  research. It contains approximately 1,000 human-annotated pairs
  (released as 997 rows across train/validation/test splits, annotated by a
  professional signer) and 3,000 synthetically generated pairs produced with
  rule-based morphological transformation, masked-token substitution, and a
  rule-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation pipeline.
